CPython for Python code cells (docs/adr/0179, docs/adr/0180)

Source:  https://www.python.org/ftp/python/3.14.7/Python-3.14.7.tar.xz
Version: VERSION (3.14.7)
SHA256:  SHA256 (checked against the python.org release-file metadata)
License: LICENSE (PSF License Version 2 and the notices CPython ships);
         LICENSE-incorporated.rst (CPython's Doc/license.rst: software CPython
         incorporates, e.g. expat and libmpdec); HACL-LICENSE (the MIT notice
         of the HACL* hashes, from Modules/_hacl)

The source tarball is not committed. `make` builds it with
scripts/cpython_runtime.sh into <BUILD>/cpython-<version>-<ABI>-<flags>/: a
static libpython with every buildable stdlib extension module
(MODULE_BUILDTYPE=static) against the pinned libraries in
third_party/{openssl,zlib,bzip2,xz,zstd,sqlite,libffi}, plus the pure-Python
standard library frozen by scripts/cpython_freeze_stdlib.py with the
just-built interpreter. The executable needs no stdlib directory and no system
Python. Excluded: the regression-test suite, Tk/IDLE/turtle, ensurepip/venv,
and native modules without a pinned library (curses, readline, gdbm/ndbm,
_uuid, macOS _scproxy, which a frozen shim replaces). No ensurepip wheels,
test modules, mimalloc, remote-debug attach or libintl are built.
`make fetch-cpython` downloads the pinned tarballs (a hash mismatch always
fails); CPYTHON_TARBALL=/path and CPYTHON_DEPS_DIR=/dir supply local copies,
and CPYTHON_FETCH=0 forbids any download.

To update: change VERSION and SHA256 together from python.org metadata,
refresh LICENSE and LICENSE-incorporated.rst (Doc/license.rst) from the new
tarball, rebuild, and rerun `make test`, the Python conformance cases and the
import sweep in docs/verification/host-code-mode/.
